%description:

TcpCubic.c:rfc9438 -- the window regains its size at the loss after K = cbrt(W_max * (1 - beta) / C).

The claim (TcpCubic.ned): "scaling constant C of the cubic window-growth curve (RFC 9438
section 4.2)".

The classes: rfc9438 (0.4, the default, the value of RFC 9438), other (another value above 0),
invalid (0 and less). The code: at the start of an epoch, K = cbrt((W_max - cwnd) / C)
(TcpCubic::update()). This test separates "rfc9438" from the other value: K moves with the cube root of 1 / C.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic and without SACK, which sends 100000 bytes; the round
trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the 15th data segment once, at a window of about 40
segments. Observation: level 3, the time K of the epoch after the loss is about 3 s; the curve
itself needs seconds to show on the wire.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.c
%# class: rfc9438
%# value: 0.4
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.c
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpCubicCRfc9438")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 100000")
             .first()
                  .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.cubic_K >= 2.4 && state.cubic_K <= 4.2")
             .describe("the ACK of the last byte, with K of the epoch after the loss")
             .within(6.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicCRfc9438 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.c = 0.4    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpCubicCRfc9438: PASS
